      "id": 1,
      "text": "South Park incorporated on December 9 1902 and joined Seattle on May 3 1907 after a 181‑36 vote.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Park%2C_Seattle",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Georgetown owned water mains that ran through South Park but refused to supply them, sparking a court battle that helped secure annexation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        25,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Park%2C_Seattle",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Grant Street Electric Railway crossed a wooden drawbridge over the Duwamish River into South Park, linking it to Seattle in the early 1900s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.seattle.gov/cityarchives/exhibits-and-education/online-exhibits/annexed-cities/south-park",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "South Park sits just south of Georgetown across the Duwamish River, a fact that inspired its name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Park%2C_Seattle",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In its early days, South Park was a small town of Italian and Japanese farmers who shipped fresh produce to Seattle’s Pike Place Market.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
